    {
      "type": "instruction",
      "text": "Nothing can take the place of reading-no lecture or image on a screen has the same power to enlighten. Pictures are a most valuable means of illustrating a written text, but they hardly enable us to form general ideas. Films, like the spoken word, flow by and are lost to us. Books abide, as life-long companions."
